1) useState() -> It allows you to create and manage a state variable in a React functional component.
syntax - 

const [stateVariable, setStateFunction] = useState(initialValue);

stateVariable: The current value.
setStateFunction: Function to update the value.
initialValue: The starting value (e.g. 0, "", false, [], {}).

